{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared golden vectors for DayResolver. Loaded by BOTH the Android (JVM) and iOS",
    "(Swift) suites. The logical day boundary decides which day every entry belongs to,",
    "so a divergence here would silently corrupt every downstream figure.",
    "resolve: epochMillis is absolute; zoneId is an IANA identifier. Cases cover DST",
    "spring-forward/fall-back and cross-timezone instants.",
    "firstDayOfWeekIso: languageTag is BCP-47; expected is an ISO-8601 weekday number",
    "(1 = Monday ... 7 = Sunday), the scheme Kotlin's WeekFields returns and the one",
    "Swift converts to from Calendar.firstWeekday, which counts Sunday as 1. The four",
    "regions are the ones whose week convention is settled: three that open on Monday",
    "and one that opens on Sunday, so both branches of the Swift conversion are hit.",
    "The number feeds the calendar grid's column order and the weekday histogram's bar",
    "order, so a divergence rotates one platform's week against the other's.",
    "",
    "calendarDate: the CALENDAR date an instant falls on in a zone — what the entry",
    "dialog shows beside a night-hour time that instantOnLogicalDate placed on the",
    "following calendar day (v0.86.0)."
  ],
